ArduPilot SITL plane: optional mass, inertia and electric propulsion from the json model.

Local cert-env change (not upstream), applied to ArduPilot d9c5097. Upstream SIM_Plane fixes
mass at 2 kg, uses torque directly as angular acceleration, makes thrust linear in throttle
(full throttle = weight / 0.7, independent of airspeed) and models battery current as
50 A * throttle^2. With this patch a model json may add:
  mass, inertia[3]                          replace the 2 kg / unit-inertia defaults
  num_motors, motor_kv, motor_R, motor_I0,  DC motor per motor
  esc_eff, prop_diameter, prop_ct[3],       propeller Ct/Cp as quadratics in advance ratio J
  prop_cp[3], prop_J_max, batt_R            SITL battery (SoC + sag) supplies the bus voltage
  launch_accel, launch_time                 launcher (catapult) push, like the -catapult frame
                                            suffix but with the model's own push and duration
Models without these keys behave exactly as before.
Also replaces SITL's turbulence model (SITL/SIM_Aircraft.cpp update_wind). The old one advanced
the horizontal gust azimuth by `2 * rand()` every physics step: that overflows signed int, so the
azimuth became ~1e9 degrees and cosf/sinf of ~1e7 radians carried no precision. The horizontal
gust direction was therefore uncorrelated at the full frame rate (measured correlation time: one
timestep) while only its magnitude was filtered, its std came out at sigma/sqrt(2) instead of
sigma, and the IIR coefficient was fixed at 0.98 per step so the spectrum depended on SIM_RATE_HZ.
Feeding that near-white gust to a quasi-steady aerodynamic model produced spurious energy: with
SIM_WIND_TURB 2 a Believer cruised on 17%% less power than in still air. Replaced with an
exponentially correlated (Ornstein-Uhlenbeck) gust in each earth-frame axis, exactly discretised
so the std is SIM_WIND_TURB at any frame rate, with the correlation length taken from the
MIL-F-8785C Dryden integral scale (height above ground below 305 m, 533 m above, floored at 10 m)
and the correlation time that length over airspeed.
Also backports the upstream master fix for the SITL pitot (AP_HAL_SITL/sitl_airspeed.cpp): 4.7.3
divides the already-equivalent pitot airspeed by EAS2TAS a second time, so the simulated sensor
under-reads by that factor (~2.8% at 590 m AMSL) and the aircraft flies faster than commanded.

Apply:   git -C src/ardupilot apply ../../patches/ardupilot-sitl-plane-electric-propulsion.patch
Build:   (cd src/ardupilot && ./waf plane)

